,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331829237,"data":"Best Practices:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331830548,"data":"- Use sympy for exact symbolic answers when possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331831859,"data":"- Use numpy for numerical verification and large-scale computation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331833201,"data":"- Combine symbolic and numerical approaches: derive symbolically, verify numerically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331834396,"data":"- Document your computational strategy clearly\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331835525,"data":"- Validate computational results against known cases or theoretical bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331836751,"data":"- For very large exponents (e.g. a^(n!)), use pow(base, exp, mod) or analytical methods — never materialize the full number\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331838224,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331839268,"data":"# Code Robustness Rules:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331840402,"data":"- Each code cell must be SELF-CONTAINED: re-import and re-define everything you need. If a previous cell errored, its definitions are LOST.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331841744,"data":"- Avoid sympy expressions that grow beyond a few hundred characters. If an expression is exploding, switch to numerical methods (numpy) or modular arithmetic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.33184323,"data":"- For geometry: prefer numpy coordinate models with brute-force verification over pure symbolic or direction-counting approaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.3318445,"data":"- For combinatorics counting: always verify no duplicates — check injectivity explicitly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.33184573,"data":"- If 5+ code cells without progress, STOP and restart with a different approach.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331847958,"data":"- When using Python, prefer converting sympy expressions to int() before passing to Python builtins like pow(), min(), max().\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331849379,"data":"- Common import: from sympy.ntheory.modular import crt (note: sympy.crt does not exist).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331850601,"data":"- If a code cell fails, re-import necessary libraries in the next cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331851796,"data":"- sympy.solve() often times out on complex systems. For polynomial systems with \u003e 3 unknowns, prefer numerical methods (scipy fsolve/minimize) or manual algebraic reduction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.33185341,"data":"- Never call sympy.simplify() or sympy.expand() on expressions involving large binomials or products of many terms. Use float() first to check the numerical value.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":519.331890016,"data":"\n"}
